<title>USA: N.Y. Dorm Authority repriced, yields cut.</title>
<headline>N.Y. Dorm Authority repriced, yields cut.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>First Albany Corp. said Wednesday it repriced New York Dormitory Authority $67 million bond deal, lowering yields in several maturities.</p>
<p>The repricing follows:</p>
<p>DORMITORY AUTHORITY OF THE STATE OF NEW YORK</p>
<p>RE: $66,740,000*</p>
<p>ROCHESTER INSTITUTE OF TECHNOLOGY</p>
<p>INSURED REVENUE BONDS, SERIES 1997</p>
<p>VERBAL AWARD.</p>
<p>PLEASE NOTE THE PRICE CHANGES IN 1999-2000, 2004, 2006-2007,</p>
<p>2010, 2017 AND 2022. ALSO, PLEASE NOTE THE ADDITION OF THE NEW</p>
<p>MATURITY</p>
<p>THE ACCOUNT IS CLOSED.</p>
<p>MOODY'S: Aaa		   S&amp;P: AAA</p>
<p>	   (UNDER A1)		 (UNDER A+)</p>
<p>MBIA INSURED</p>
<p>DATED: 07/01/1997	    FIRST COUPON: 01/01/1998</p>
<p>DUE: 07/01</p>
<p> MATURITY		AMOUNT*    COUPON	   PRICE</p>
<p>07/01/1998		   10M    4.25  %	  4.00</p>
